WEBVTT

00:00:23.208 --> 00:00:25.375
"Rui Minaduki"

00:00:28.208 --> 00:00:29.625
Summer's here.

00:00:30.583 --> 00:00:33.167
It's gearing up to be a special one, too.

00:00:41.125 --> 00:00:43.417
"You Haduki"
"Yoru Nagatsuki"

00:00:48.417 --> 00:00:50.250
"Kakeru Shiwasu"
"So beautiful!"

00:00:50.250 --> 00:00:52.292
"Koi Kisaragi"
"Looks delicious!"

00:00:54.042 --> 00:00:56.042
"No eating allowed!"

00:00:57.250 --> 00:00:59.792
"Arata Uduki"

00:01:01.958 --> 00:01:04.292
"Haru Yayoi"

00:01:12.375 --> 00:01:15.333
We came to this island yesterday.

00:01:15.333 --> 00:01:20.333
The members of Gravi and Procella
are here filming a joint music video.

00:01:25.000 --> 00:01:27.125
Yesss!

00:01:27.125 --> 00:01:28.458
Yay!

00:01:28.458 --> 00:01:30.667
We've gone and fired them up.

00:01:30.667 --> 00:01:33.458
We've still got some fight in us.
We'll finish this.

00:01:33.458 --> 00:01:35.208
Yeah! Let's do our best!

00:01:35.250 --> 00:01:36.333
"Iku Kannaduki"

00:01:36.583 --> 00:01:36.833
"Aoi Satsuki"

00:01:36.833 --> 00:01:38.000
"Aoi Satsuki"
Kakeru!

00:01:39.792 --> 00:01:40.792
You!

00:01:43.500 --> 00:01:44.625
"Kai Fuduki"

00:01:52.375 --> 00:01:54.583
Yay!

00:01:54.583 --> 00:01:57.292
The losers are on meal duty today!

00:01:57.292 --> 00:01:59.167
A man never goes back on his word.

00:01:59.167 --> 00:02:02.042
We haven't lost yet!

00:02:02.042 --> 00:02:05.125
Sorry, but we'll be winning this one, Aoi.

00:02:08.750 --> 00:02:09.292
Time out!

00:02:09.292 --> 00:02:10.250
Huh?

00:02:10.250 --> 00:02:11.500
Oh!

00:02:11.500 --> 00:02:12.542
"Hajime Mutsuki"
We're swapping players.

00:02:15.958 --> 00:02:17.750
Are they almost done?

00:02:17.750 --> 00:02:18.708
It looks that way.

00:02:18.708 --> 00:02:22.167
Then I'll go grab a shower.

00:02:22.167 --> 00:02:24.250
Sure, go right ahead.

00:02:33.542 --> 00:02:35.875
So the Black King has arrived.

00:02:35.875 --> 00:02:39.667
A win against Hajime means
a total Procella victory!

00:02:39.667 --> 00:02:41.583
Give it all you've got, Iku!

00:02:41.583 --> 00:02:43.042
You bet!

00:02:48.792 --> 00:02:51.042
W-Wow...

00:02:51.042 --> 00:02:53.958
Hey, the other side is giving it their all, too!

00:02:53.958 --> 00:02:57.917
That scored a little too high
for a back attack, Hajime!

00:02:57.917 --> 00:02:59.208
Time out!

00:02:59.208 --> 00:02:59.375
"Shun Shimotsuki"

00:02:59.375 --> 00:03:00.833
"Shun Shimotsuki"
Iku, switch with me.

00:03:00.833 --> 00:03:02.542
"Shun Shimotsuki"
Huh? Oh, okay!

00:03:06.417 --> 00:03:10.875
I've got to receive Hajime's ball
for this to be picture-perfect.

00:03:10.875 --> 00:03:14.458
Just keep telling yourself that!

00:03:14.458 --> 00:03:15.500
Oof!

00:03:17.083 --> 00:03:18.958
Aoi!

00:03:18.958 --> 00:03:20.417
A time-differential attack, on sand?!

00:03:20.417 --> 00:03:21.833
And so <i>fast</i>!

00:03:39.708 --> 00:03:41.917
Shun's really working.

00:03:41.917 --> 00:03:44.833
He's reaching higher and higher levels, all right.

00:03:44.833 --> 00:03:47.583
It's not often <i>you </i>exercise.

00:03:48.542 --> 00:03:53.583
I told you: my role is to receive your love.

00:03:53.583 --> 00:03:55.958
Can you please cut this scene?

00:03:55.958 --> 00:03:56.917
What?!

00:03:56.917 --> 00:03:59.000
Receive the <i>ball</i>, not my <i>love</i>.

00:03:59.000 --> 00:04:02.750
Okay, okay. Please delete that, folks!

00:04:02.750 --> 00:04:08.292
All right, now it's our turn.
Here goes, Hajime: my killer serve!

00:04:08.292 --> 00:04:10.417
K-Killer serve?

00:04:10.417 --> 00:04:11.917
This won't end well.

00:04:11.917 --> 00:04:15.708
Behold: The Eternal Icicle Serve!

00:04:25.833 --> 00:04:28.458
Filming went on without a hitch.

00:04:28.458 --> 00:04:34.792
We had our fill of the summer,
the island, the ocean--

00:04:34.792 --> 00:04:36.250
all while working.

00:04:46.792 --> 00:04:50.375
<i>Fluttering and dancing in the sky</i>

00:04:50.375 --> 00:04:56.750
<i>Let our love reach you...</i>

00:04:56.750 --> 00:04:57.500
<i>LOVE,</i>

00:04:57.500 --> 00:04:58.583
<i>LOVE,</i>

00:04:58.583 --> 00:05:00.000
<i>LOVE...</i>

00:05:02.208 --> 00:05:04.042
<i>ohhhh... SAY!</i>

00:05:04.042 --> 00:05:05.458
<i>This heart</i>

00:05:05.458 --> 00:05:07.708
<i>Try and move it</i>

00:05:07.708 --> 00:05:10.833
<i>Look, how should I show you?</i>

00:05:10.833 --> 00:05:12.000
<i>Then together with us</i>

00:05:12.000 --> 00:05:13.375
<i>Let's dance! Take my hand</i>

00:05:13.375 --> 00:05:14.833
<i>hey yeah yeah!</i>

00:05:14.833 --> 00:05:16.333
<i>Leave it to me</i>

00:05:16.333 --> 00:05:19.250
<i>to escort you! ALL RIGHT!</i>

00:05:19.250 --> 00:05:22.000
<i>As if worrying, the passing rain</i>

00:05:22.000 --> 00:05:25.458
<i>caressed my cheek gently,</i>
<i>so as not to be noticed.</i>

00:05:25.458 --> 00:05:29.417
<i>Jumping over faster than a shooting star</i>

00:05:29.417 --> 00:05:32.875
<i>Reach out your hand!</i>

00:05:32.875 --> 00:05:33.792
<i>let's get LOVE!</i>

00:05:33.792 --> 00:05:35.417
<i>Shout to the moon! (shout!)</i>

00:05:35.417 --> 00:05:37.042
<i>Let your shout ring out! (shout!)</i>

00:05:37.042 --> 00:05:38.208
<i>What's up, what's up?</i>

00:05:38.208 --> 00:05:39.958
<i>Let me hear your voice</i>

00:05:39.958 --> 00:05:41.500
<i>Undo your hair</i>

00:05:41.500 --> 00:05:44.500
<i>Saying goodbye to yesterday</i>

00:05:44.500 --> 00:05:45.500
<i>when my eyes were closed</i>

00:05:45.500 --> 00:05:48.042
<i>A single petal fluttering lightly</i>

00:05:48.042 --> 00:05:49.875
<i>Spit it out, SHOUT! (shout!)</i>

00:05:49.875 --> 00:05:51.708
<i>Shout out your feelings! (shout!)</i>

00:05:51.708 --> 00:05:52.458
<i>Isn't it fine</i>

00:05:52.458 --> 00:05:54.583
<i>if nothing is for sure?</i>

00:05:54.583 --> 00:05:55.625
<i>wow yeah!</i>

00:05:55.625 --> 00:05:56.125
<i>That's right</i>

00:05:56.125 --> 00:05:57.958
<i>Let's put away the lies</i>

00:05:57.958 --> 00:06:00.667
<i>Let lots of love reach you</i>

00:06:05.208 --> 00:06:07.625
<i>Let lots of love reach you</i>

00:06:16.375 --> 00:06:20.500
"A Smart Detective!?"

00:06:21.417 --> 00:06:23.292
Nice work today!

00:06:31.833 --> 00:06:33.417
A job well done!

00:06:33.417 --> 00:06:37.125
Filming finished with no problems,
thanks to all of you.

00:06:37.125 --> 00:06:42.083
Now, tomorrow was supposed to be
a backup day for filming,

00:06:42.083 --> 00:06:44.792
but you're completely off the clock
until we leave the day after.

00:06:44.792 --> 00:06:46.667
Hooray!

00:06:46.667 --> 00:06:50.500
But please don't head into town.

00:06:50.500 --> 00:06:53.875
With so many of you on the move,
you're bound to stand out.

00:06:53.875 --> 00:06:55.792
Okay!

00:06:55.792 --> 00:06:59.708
We have work to do, so we'll
head back to the hotel in town.

00:06:59.708 --> 00:07:03.542
We'll come pick you up in two days,
when it's time to leave.

00:07:03.542 --> 00:07:05.417
--See you later!
--Thanks again!

00:07:05.417 --> 00:07:09.625
We were in a pretty good mood at that point.

00:07:09.625 --> 00:07:13.458
We could never have dreamed
such an incident would befall us.

00:07:15.167 --> 00:07:18.042
Weren't those outfits a little much?

00:07:18.042 --> 00:07:20.167
As long as they go over well, right?

00:07:20.167 --> 00:07:21.833
It's none of my business.

00:07:21.833 --> 00:07:24.583
Oh, hey, I took a picture. Can I upload it?

00:07:24.583 --> 00:07:26.500
Anything but that!

00:07:31.833 --> 00:07:33.000
What happened?!

00:07:33.000 --> 00:07:34.500
What on earth--

00:07:44.208 --> 00:07:46.583
Haru's essence...

00:07:46.583 --> 00:07:47.875
This is terrible...

00:07:47.875 --> 00:07:50.083
Haru! Oh, you're a mess!

00:07:50.083 --> 00:07:55.167
No, my <i>glasses </i>are a mess, not me!

00:07:55.167 --> 00:07:57.250
Truly a great loss.

00:07:57.250 --> 00:07:58.917
Our condolences, Haru.

00:07:58.917 --> 00:07:59.833
Shake it off.

00:07:59.833 --> 00:08:02.083
Just look at them: cold and dead!

00:08:02.083 --> 00:08:03.833
Come on, now.

00:08:07.292 --> 00:08:12.625
How amusing. Leave this
puzzler of a case entirely to me!

00:08:12.625 --> 00:08:16.125
On my grandmother's name, I will see
the single truth for what it is!

00:08:16.125 --> 00:08:19.375
He looks like a young boy,
but has a head full of little grey cells!

00:08:20.583 --> 00:08:22.333
"Detective Koikku"
His name? Detective Koikku!

00:08:22.333 --> 00:08:24.208
That's a real mish-mash!

00:08:24.208 --> 00:08:27.542
Wow, they really are broken right in two.

00:08:27.542 --> 00:08:30.333
So it was someone capable
of snapping them like that...

00:08:30.333 --> 00:08:30.875
--My, my, my.

00:08:30.875 --> 00:08:32.958
--Um, hello?
--My, my, my.

00:08:32.958 --> 00:08:34.125
Are you listening?

00:08:34.125 --> 00:08:35.958
Shake it off, Koi.

00:08:42.833 --> 00:08:44.792
Who saw Haru last?

00:08:44.792 --> 00:08:46.833
Haru's right here, you know.

00:08:46.833 --> 00:08:49.292
When did you remove your alter ego, anyway?

00:08:49.292 --> 00:08:53.000
My alter ego? It's called
"taking off my glasses!"

00:08:53.000 --> 00:08:57.667
Let's see, I came back from the beach
and took them off to shower.

00:08:58.667 --> 00:09:02.000
And who first discovered
Haru's tragic situation?

00:09:02.000 --> 00:09:02.958
That was me.

00:09:02.958 --> 00:09:06.750
I see. So Haru's the one who found Haru...

00:09:06.750 --> 00:09:09.500
You're sticking with that setup
no matter what, I see.

00:09:10.500 --> 00:09:14.125
After the discovery, who was
the first in the living room?

00:09:14.125 --> 00:09:16.875
Hajime was the first one here.

00:09:16.875 --> 00:09:21.292
Right. I was meeting with Shun
in a room in the back,

00:09:21.292 --> 00:09:23.417
but I came down when I heard your voice.

00:09:26.417 --> 00:09:30.917
And what time had you come back
to the cottage, Haru?

00:09:30.917 --> 00:09:33.167
I figured there'd be a line for the shower,

00:09:33.167 --> 00:09:36.583
so I left the beach earlier than everyone else...

00:09:36.583 --> 00:09:39.333
It was when I came to check on you.

00:09:39.333 --> 00:09:42.125
About what time was that, Yoru?

00:09:42.125 --> 00:09:45.833
I remember hearing the
top-of-the-hour tone on the radio,

00:09:49.792 --> 00:09:53.375
so... We were done filming the beach
volleyball game before 4.

00:09:55.792 --> 00:09:59.042
So the radio's hour tone
would have been for 3 o'clock.

00:09:59.042 --> 00:10:03.417
After I came back to the cottage,
I took a shower and rested a while.

00:10:03.417 --> 00:10:07.333
I noticed my glasses were missing
and started looking for them at about 5.

00:10:07.333 --> 00:10:09.833
That's when everyone gathered just now.

00:10:11.750 --> 00:10:16.750
I need everyone to tell me where
they were between 3 and 5 o'clock.

00:10:16.750 --> 00:10:20.500
I'm investigating your alibis.

00:10:20.500 --> 00:10:22.292
Oh, Iku, you help, too.

00:10:22.292 --> 00:10:23.833
Huh? Me?

00:10:23.833 --> 00:10:28.042
A great detective must have
a great assistant, Watson.

00:10:29.583 --> 00:10:31.000
Got it.

00:10:32.125 --> 00:10:33.333
"Arata Uduki's Testimony"

00:10:35.083 --> 00:10:39.833
Me and the other beach
volleyball players were filming till 4.

00:10:39.833 --> 00:10:43.417
Then Hajime and Shun went off for a meeting.

00:10:43.417 --> 00:10:44.875
Mm-hmm, mm-hmm...

00:10:44.875 --> 00:10:48.417
Aoi, Kakeru, and I were
messing around with you.

00:10:48.417 --> 00:10:51.583
So that <i>was </i>you guys!

00:10:51.583 --> 00:10:54.167
I lie down for a nap, and the
next thing I know, I'm buried!

00:10:54.167 --> 00:10:56.958
I just <i>know </i>you took some awful photos, too!

00:11:00.417 --> 00:11:03.125
So Gravi's alibis are in place.

00:11:03.125 --> 00:11:05.292
All that's left... is Procella.

00:11:05.292 --> 00:11:05.958
"Yoru Nagatsuki's Testimony"

00:11:05.958 --> 00:11:08.375
"Yoru Nagatsuki's Testimony"
What did you do after Haru left?

00:11:08.375 --> 00:11:10.292
I didn't have anything in particular to do,

00:11:10.292 --> 00:11:14.125
so Rui and I took a cart to
the shop in the center of the island.

00:11:19.292 --> 00:11:19.833
"Rui Minaduki's Testimony"

00:11:19.833 --> 00:11:21.667
"Rui Minaduki's Testimony"
I was with Yoru. We bought souvenirs.

00:11:21.667 --> 00:11:23.250
I was with Yoru. We bought souvenirs.

00:11:23.250 --> 00:11:24.042
Here.

00:11:24.042 --> 00:11:26.292
"*Storing This Receipt: If kept in a wallet,
please fold so the printed surface is on the inside."

00:11:26.542 --> 00:11:28.583
Did you meet anyone on the way?

00:11:28.583 --> 00:11:29.625
No.

00:11:29.625 --> 00:11:32.167
Pass anyone in the cart?

00:11:32.167 --> 00:11:35.708
Oh... we saw You's cart on the way back.

00:11:36.917 --> 00:11:38.333
Later!

00:11:41.042 --> 00:11:42.042
"You Haduki's Testimony"

00:11:42.042 --> 00:11:45.125
We were on meal duty since
we lost the volleyball game,

00:11:45.125 --> 00:11:49.958
so Kai and Iku and I went to
the island store to shop for dinner.

00:11:49.958 --> 00:11:53.625
We were going to make curry,
but we were missing carrots and stuff.

00:11:53.625 --> 00:11:56.208
Iku, this important detail...

00:11:56.208 --> 00:11:58.792
Yeah, I forgot to mention that.

00:12:01.583 --> 00:12:05.208
Huh? Everyone has an alibi.

00:12:06.625 --> 00:12:08.583
I know who the culprit is!

00:12:10.125 --> 00:12:11.208
Come in!

00:12:11.208 --> 00:12:15.750
How's it going, detectives?
Figured out the culprit yet?

00:12:15.750 --> 00:12:16.750
Yes!

00:12:18.083 --> 00:12:21.583
It's fun to chase down something you can't see.

00:12:21.583 --> 00:12:28.208
But over time, the pursuit of the truth
may invite new misfortune.

00:12:28.208 --> 00:12:30.125
What does that mean?

00:12:31.958 --> 00:12:36.625
It <i>can </i>be happier never to arrive
at a clear-cut resolution.

00:12:37.750 --> 00:12:40.750
Are you saying we should stop
our search for the culprit?

00:12:41.875 --> 00:12:46.625
I wonder. I leave the final call
up to our detectives.

00:12:49.000 --> 00:12:50.000
Okay...

00:12:55.917 --> 00:12:57.708
I know who did it.

00:12:59.083 --> 00:13:01.875
Everyone here has an alibi,

00:13:01.875 --> 00:13:04.833
so the culprit is someone who's <i>not </i>here.

00:13:04.833 --> 00:13:08.000
That is... the two managers!

00:13:08.000 --> 00:13:09.833
What?!

00:13:09.833 --> 00:13:12.000
"Connected" "Mr. Tsukishiro"
What? I don't know anything

00:13:12.000 --> 00:13:13.500
"Connected" "Mr. Tsukishiro"
about any glasses.

00:13:13.500 --> 00:13:17.708
Alibis? We've been with
the staff this whole time.

00:13:19.250 --> 00:13:22.875
...Just kidding.

00:13:22.875 --> 00:13:24.083
Ha ha...

00:13:26.208 --> 00:13:31.167
N-No, I mean, if everyone has an alibi,
it <i>has </i>to be someone else!

00:13:36.750 --> 00:13:38.875
There is only one truth.

00:13:41.083 --> 00:13:45.250
And sure as anything, a member
who isn't here knows what that is.

00:13:48.083 --> 00:13:50.000
A member who isn't here...

00:13:51.583 --> 00:13:52.750
Hajime?

00:13:52.750 --> 00:14:02.375
Hajime!

00:14:13.792 --> 00:14:17.208
This was the beginning
of a whole new tragedy.

00:14:25.458 --> 00:14:26.875
"*For illustration purposes"

00:14:26.875 --> 00:14:30.292
"*For illustration purposes"
Where could Hajime have gone?

00:14:30.292 --> 00:14:33.375
Don't tell me he's the culprit!

00:14:33.375 --> 00:14:39.458
I can't imagine Hajime would so
carelessly break someone's things.

00:14:40.917 --> 00:14:45.292
It happened right when we came back.

00:14:45.292 --> 00:14:48.667
There was a pillow by the living room entrance,

00:14:48.667 --> 00:14:51.458
and when I stepped on it,
the glasses came out from underneath.

00:14:52.500 --> 00:14:56.792
I was going to apologize to Haru
when he finished showering.

00:15:01.208 --> 00:15:06.083
I wanted to replace my damp towel
before we went shopping, when...

00:15:08.667 --> 00:15:10.750
Ack!

00:15:10.750 --> 00:15:13.583
And since that was dangerous,
I gathered up the pieces

00:15:13.583 --> 00:15:16.208
and moved them to the kitchen.

00:15:16.208 --> 00:15:18.292
What, no carrots?

00:15:18.292 --> 00:15:20.333
When I casually picked up the towel...

00:15:22.167 --> 00:15:24.458
We thought the island shop might be closing,

00:15:24.458 --> 00:15:26.333
so I set them aside for the time being.

00:15:27.958 --> 00:15:32.833
Hey, Iku, why don't you and Kai
come with me to shop for dinner?

00:15:32.833 --> 00:15:34.083
Okay!

00:15:35.083 --> 00:15:37.167
That's not where I left them...

00:15:39.083 --> 00:15:41.958
That isn't where we left them!

00:15:41.958 --> 00:15:45.792
But that's not where I left them...

00:15:50.375 --> 00:15:52.625
Okay. Got it.

00:16:01.667 --> 00:16:07.417
That was Hajime. He wants us
to meet in the cottage's backyard.

00:16:07.417 --> 00:16:10.708
He said he'd tell us everything.

00:16:17.958 --> 00:16:18.667
Hajime!

00:16:18.667 --> 00:16:19.292
Hajime...

00:16:19.292 --> 00:16:20.625
--Hajime!
--Hajime!

00:16:20.625 --> 00:16:21.958
--Hajime!
--Hajime!

00:16:21.958 --> 00:16:22.625
Hajime!

00:16:22.625 --> 00:16:24.125
--Hajime!
--Hajime.

00:16:24.125 --> 00:16:25.375
Hajime!

00:16:25.375 --> 00:16:26.750
Hajime.

00:16:27.750 --> 00:16:31.333
Sorry for calling you all here.

00:16:31.333 --> 00:16:36.875
Was it you, Hajime? The one who broke
Haru--I mean, Haru's essence?

00:16:39.542 --> 00:16:40.792
It wasn't me.

00:16:40.792 --> 00:16:43.583
Then, what on earth did you want to tell us?

00:16:52.083 --> 00:16:56.000
Hajime, let's call it off.

00:16:56.000 --> 00:16:59.167
Haru's essence fell on the floor and broke.

00:16:59.167 --> 00:17:00.583
That's good enough.

00:17:03.417 --> 00:17:07.250
If it'll end this without
anyone feeling guilty, that is.

00:17:07.250 --> 00:17:11.375
Hajime, tell us the truth. Otherwise, I won't...

00:17:11.375 --> 00:17:16.333
...no, my essence won't be
able to rest in peace. Ever.

00:17:16.333 --> 00:17:18.458
Finally! He called it "essence" himse--!

00:17:19.667 --> 00:17:22.917
Enough nonsense. The truth is...

00:17:40.958 --> 00:17:44.292
The truth is... this.

00:17:46.250 --> 00:17:47.917
What?!

00:17:47.917 --> 00:17:52.083
He must have snuck into
ဆ

00:17:52.083 --> 00:17:54.625
This whole trip?!

00:18:00.333 --> 00:18:01.750
"Detective Koikku: Koi Kisaraki
The Great Assistant: Iku Kannaduki"

00:18:01.750 --> 00:18:03.042
"Kakeru Shiwasu: Kakeru Shiwasu
Hajime Mutsuki: Hajime Mutsuki"

00:18:03.042 --> 00:18:04.375
"Haru Yayoi (Eyeglass Holder): Haru Yayoi
Arata Uduki: Arata Uduki"

00:18:04.375 --> 00:18:05.750
"Aoi Satsuki: Aoi Satsuki
Rui Minaduki: Rui Minaduki"

00:18:05.750 --> 00:18:06.917
"Kai Fuduki: Kai Fuduki
You Haduki: You Haduki"

00:18:06.917 --> 00:18:10.042
"Yoru Nagatsuki: Yoru Nagatsuki
Shun Shimotsuki: Shun Shimotsuki"

00:18:10.708 --> 00:18:13.458
"The Real Culprit: Kuroda
Haru Yayoi (Essence): The Broken Glasses"

00:18:16.042 --> 00:18:20.917
Kuroda, we'll be filming all over
while we're at this cottage.

00:18:20.917 --> 00:18:24.583
Do <i>not </i>leave this room until
we're done with work, okay?

00:19:02.125 --> 00:19:04.583
I didn't notice until it was too late.

00:19:07.792 --> 00:19:09.833
Kuroda was asleep.

00:19:11.000 --> 00:19:12.958
I cleaned up the carrots...

00:19:19.667 --> 00:19:22.833
...and carried Kuroda to
my room on the second floor.

00:19:23.958 --> 00:19:25.375
We're home!

00:19:33.875 --> 00:19:37.042
I knew we'd bought
the ingredients for curry.

00:19:37.042 --> 00:19:41.208
It was weird that carrots were
the only thing we were out of.

00:19:41.208 --> 00:19:43.375
So I put two and two together.

00:19:44.542 --> 00:19:49.000
I should have told everyone
my deduction earlier,

00:19:49.000 --> 00:19:52.375
but then Koi started
having fun playing detective.

00:19:52.375 --> 00:19:54.250
What, me?

00:19:54.250 --> 00:19:59.750
Yes, I wanted your ace detective
work to solve this uneventfully.

00:19:59.750 --> 00:20:04.875
But then the glasses started
moving around, beginning with Kakeru.

00:20:04.875 --> 00:20:09.792
I put them back where they were
so as not to confuse things.

00:20:11.583 --> 00:20:15.458
That sent Koi's deductions
into a dead end instead.

00:20:15.458 --> 00:20:20.083
So I went to my room
to have Kuroda confess, but...

00:20:20.083 --> 00:20:22.583
Kuroda had escaped.

00:20:22.583 --> 00:20:27.375
Who knew it would come to <i>this</i>
while I was out looking for him?

00:20:28.458 --> 00:20:33.083
So to sum up, this incident was no one's fault.

00:20:33.083 --> 00:20:35.208
It was just an unfortunate accident.

00:20:35.208 --> 00:20:36.667
I see!

00:20:37.667 --> 00:20:39.042
Sheesh.

00:20:39.042 --> 00:20:43.958
Koi and I were tearing our hair out,
all "It can't be Hajime!"

00:20:45.000 --> 00:20:47.208
Hey! Kuroda!

00:20:47.208 --> 00:20:50.458
And you <i>do </i>put your glasses
in just any old place, Haru.

00:20:50.458 --> 00:20:55.042
Still, he could have come forward
a lot sooner! Honestly!

00:20:55.042 --> 00:20:56.208
Hey!

00:20:56.208 --> 00:20:58.083
Wait! Kuroda!

00:21:29.750 --> 00:21:32.917
I smell another mystery.

00:21:32.917 --> 00:21:35.792
No, <i>this </i>is purely an accident.

00:21:44.208 --> 00:21:53.333
<i>I'm sure it's because of you</i>
<i>that I can keep walking on</i>

00:21:53.333 --> 00:21:57.292
<i>That's true from now on, too</i>

00:22:07.708 --> 00:22:11.875
<i>My smartphone alarm didn't go off.</i>

00:22:11.875 --> 00:22:16.167
<i>Even if I try to lie, embarrassed</i>

00:22:16.167 --> 00:22:20.500
<i>You can tell, right?</i>
<i>With your puffed out cheeks</i>

00:22:20.500 --> 00:22:24.667
<i>Grabbing my head and tousling my hair </i>

00:22:24.667 --> 00:22:32.125
<i>Running on a seventeen degree slope</i>

00:22:32.125 --> 00:22:34.417
<i>To tomorrow</i>

00:22:34.417 --> 00:22:39.333
<i>Opening my eyes wide to etch</i>
<i>the moment into my mind</i>

00:22:39.333 --> 00:22:43.708
<i>The sky, the city, and that face--everything</i>

00:22:43.708 --> 00:22:52.500
<i>I'm sure it's because of you</i>
<i>that even though I wavered</i>

00:22:52.500 --> 00:22:57.125
<i>I was able to make it here</i>

00:23:11.917 --> 00:23:13.208
"Episode 7: The Hajime Mutsuki Expedition"

00:23:13.208 --> 00:23:14.833
"Episode 7: The Hajime Mutsuki Expedition"
Emergency operation!

00:23:14.833 --> 00:23:17.458
"Episode 7: The Hajime Mutsuki Expedition"
Twelve young men stranded on a solitary isle

00:23:17.458 --> 00:23:19.000
"Episode 7: The Hajime Mutsuki Expedition"
in the middle of the sea!

00:23:19.000 --> 00:23:22.792
The roars of wild beasts echo
through the jungle at midnight...

00:23:22.792 --> 00:23:26.708
Can they manage to survive?!

00:23:26.708 --> 00:23:30.833
Next time: "Gravi and
Procella's Jungle Encounter:

00:23:30.833 --> 00:23:34.417
Exposing the True Identity of
the Mysterious Giant Creature!"

00:23:34.417 --> 00:23:35.708
Or rather:

00:23:35.708 --> 00:23:38.583
"The Hajime Mutsuki Expedition"!

00:23:38.583 --> 00:23:42.059
Titles don't lie!
